            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "The commit that introduced this claimed it was temporary:\n\n> Ief23624f4ffa36f551b313e5ffdfd8907c821057\n> After discussing with Jagpal Singh Gill, we agreed to use the proposed gpio_util instead of devmem until the liquid-valve-train topic is ready.\n\nWe should not be using debugfs; it is not considered a stable API and can change with any new kernel version.\n\nIf we have GPIOs that are busy, we need to figure out why, and add to the appropriate daemon any interaction you require."
                }
